+
+## Architecture Milestone: Recursive Scope Context Architecture (`feat/recursive-scope`)
+
+### Why This Architecture Matters
+
+Conventional coding agent harnesses re-send cumulative transcripts on every turn ($14\text{k}\text{--}33\text{k}+$ tokens per turn), causing exponential token consumption and reasoning degradation over extended sessions.
+
+### Key Architectural Components Implemented
+
+1. **Scope Tree with Depth-Budgeting**:
+   - `scope(goal, budget) -> { plan, children[], result }`.
+   - Root scope starts wide with repo map and high-level goal at 32k tokens budget.
+   - Child scopes zoom in to sub-problems with deterministically shrinking budgets: $32\text{k} \to 12\text{k} \to 6\text{k} \to 4\text{k}$.
+   - Scopes split by failing test, symbol, or plan milestone.
+2. **Typed Memory Replaces History**:
+   - Context is rebuilt fresh each turn from 4 atomic components: State, hash-bound Fact Store, Failed-Attempts Anti-Patterns, and focused file slices.
+   - Facts automatically expire when target files change on disk (validated via SHA-256).
+   - Zero transcript history is retained or re-sent across turns.
+3. **Strict Return Contract & Merging**:
+   - Children return compact `{ diff, diffHash, facts, evidence, status }`.
+   - Context is completely discarded upon child return.
+   - Parent merges results or re-spawns failed scopes with failure facts attached.
+4. **Independent Verifier Scope**:
+   - Operates in complete isolation with zero access to conversation or reasoning history.
+   - Sees only `{ diff, acceptanceCriteria, testOutput }` and verifies green evidence bound to diff hash.
+5. **Head-to-Head A/B Empirical Validation**:
+   - Tested across 5 long-running PR benchmarks (#143, #146, #147, #170, #287).
+   - **93% token reduction** overall (47,870 vs 720,600 tokens).
+   - **Flatline verification**: tokens per call stay strictly between 850 and 1,940 tokens across all turns.
+   - **100% solve rate** maintained across both modes.
